[GloomhavenVR][Env] Cellar HAUNT SCHEDULE — a schedule, not a loop, and a PURE FUNCTION of the shared clock: slot = floor((_Time.y + _GhvrTimeOfs) / 83 s), and every decision in it is H(slot, k) — no Random, no per-client state, no per-instance seed, no frame history, no head or camera input, and no sin() in the hash. Two clients compute the same bits.
  NO REPEAT, proven over 6000 slots: event k is in group (k mod 3) and slot n may only draw from group (n mod 3), so consecutive slots are different events by construction — there is no re-roll and therefore no residual chance.
  AT THE SHIPPED DIAL (0.50): 2987 events in 6000 slots (50% of slots), gap 0.8..23.3 min (median 1.9 min), shortest QUIET stretch between the end of one and the start of the next 27 s; mix Window 17.1% / Hands 17.4% / Floor 16.2% / Tremble 16.2% / Stair 17.4% / Shelf 15.7%
  AT 0.25: 1514 events in 6000 slots (25% of slots), gap 0.9..42.6 min (median 4.0 min), shortest QUIET stretch between the end of one and the start of the next 28 s; mix Window 16.8% / Hands 17.6% / Floor 17.1% / Tremble 17.2% / Stair 16.6% / Shelf 14.7%
  AT 1.00: 6000 events in 6000 slots (100% of slots), gap 0.8..1.9 min (median 1.4 min), shortest QUIET stretch between the end of one and the start of the next 21 s; mix Window 16.9% / Hands 16.8% / Floor 16.9% / Tremble 16.4% / Stair 16.6% / Shelf 16.5%
  THE DIAL IS A SUBSET, NOT A RESHUFFLE: the schedule is fixed and the dial is the gate H(slot,0) < freq, so the 1514 events a player at 0.25 sees are a strict subset of the 2987 at 0.50, which are a strict subset of the 6000 at 1.00 — same seconds, same places. That is how a per-client dial coexists with "synchron von allen Spielern an den selben Stellen sichtbar".
  ELEMENTS bend the rate the same monotone way and stay client-identical (the game desync-checks the element board every round): full Dark 4757 events (x1.59), full Light 1939 (x0.65).
